=== layout: one-panel

# Presentation Tips

@body

## Tell A Story

- Give the presentation a beginning, middle, and end.
- Respect the allotted time; once you run long, the audience starts watching the clock.
- Explain at the level of the class. Define technical terms and give novices enough introduction to follow.
- Engage the audience rather than reading slides.

=== layout: one-panel

# Presentation Tips: Design for Attention

@body

## Design For Attention

- Use note cards if needed, but do not read the slides.
- Prefer short phrases over complete sentences; break up large blocks of content.
- Try to use a meaningful picture on every slide.
- Narrate any movie yourself. A flip-book animation can explain a changing process.
- Prepare for questions. Show enthusiasm and make the case exciting.

=== layout: one-panel

# Last-Minute Priorities

@body

- Submit early enough to use the plagiarism checker and resubmit before the deadline when needed.
- Cite sources; do not copy them.
- You can polish a turd: formatting is a meaningful part of the grade, so clear visual presentation helps good ideas land.
- Spend the most effort on high-weight sections, especially the executive summary; management and investment deserve care but less time.
